# Fundraising D19 renewal scheduling

## Shipped

| Piece | Location |
|-------|----------|
| Who to email | `shouldSendRenewalNotice` (Active, lead window / 14 days past end, no intent, not already notified this term) |
| Batch send | `runFundraisingRenewalNotices` → D19 once, then `renewalNoticeSentAt` |
| Vercel Cron | `vercel.json` → `GET /api/cron/fundraising-renewal` at `0 20 * * *` (20:00 UTC ≈ morning Australia) |
| Auth | `Authorization: Bearer CRON_SECRET` (must be set in Vercel Production) |
| Admin backup | Settings → Maintenance → **Run due renewals (D19)** |
| Per-partner | Partners row → Send renewal (D19) |

Partners list does not have the batch button.

## Hobby invariant

Hobby allows **at most one run per calendar day** per cron. `*/10 * * * *` (Etsy) failed deploy and was removed in `855b126`. D19 is daily, so it is legal in `vercel.json`.

Guard: `npx tsx scripts/verify-vercel-crons-hobby.ts`

## Do not

- Add `/api/cron/etsy-sync` (or any sub-daily schedule) to `vercel.json` on Hobby
- Put the batch “Run due renewals” button back on the Partners list header without asking
- Treat missing `CRON_SECRET` as a code bug — it is a Production env var; the route returns 503 if unset
